Sheep
=====

Origin and attribution
----------------------

This project began on 2026-08-29 as a fork of an MIT-licensed C/C++ LLM
inference project. Every file that originated upstream has since been deleted:

* the tensor library and the model/graph runtime (tensor/, core/),
* the format reader and converters (pygguf/),
* the applications and their web UI (apps/), removed 2026-09-23.

What remains in the working tree is original work written for this project:

* sml/      the SSF format, quantized kernels, engine, CLI, server, GPU path
* tooling/  the quantizer, calibration, gates, benchmarks, autotuner, live agent
* brand/    logo and marks
* the documentation at the top level

The git history still contains the upstream code, at and after the baseline
commit, so the upstream copyright and permission notice is kept verbatim in
LICENSE and governs those historical revisions. Renaming files or symbols would
not have changed that; deleting them is what changes it. Both copyright lines
stand in LICENSE: the upstream authors for the history, and this project's
author for the code in the tree.

The reference engine is named in README.md, METHOD.md and RESULTS.md only to
say what was measured against what. Nothing of its code is in this tree.

Model identifiers, repository ids and download URLs are unchanged wherever they
address files hosted by third parties, because they are compared against, or
resolve to, bytes produced elsewhere.
